[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2454570453","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/98655#issuecomment-2454570453","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98655","id":2454570453,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6STcXV","user":{"login":"roalyr","id":46825200,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2ODI1MjAw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/46825200?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/roalyr","html_url":"https://github.com/roalyr","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roalyr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roalyr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roalyr/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roalyr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roalyr/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roalyr/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roalyr/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roalyr/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roalyr/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-04T12:18:47Z","updated_at":"2024-11-04T12:19:04Z","body":"I've gathered all my tweaks in a single commit for 4.x : https://github.com/godotengine/godot/compare/master...roalyr:godot-for-3d-open-worlds:master and for 3.x: https://github.com/godotengine/godot/compare/3.x...roalyr:godot-for-3d-open-worlds:3.x\r\nJust in case. I also think it is worth adding editor tweaks to the list (scene camera and in-game camera limits, editor zooming speed, grid and gizmos rendering precision, and so on).","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2454570453/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2454789078","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/98655#issuecomment-2454789078","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98655","id":2454789078,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6SURvW","user":{"login":"Zireael07","id":4525388,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1MjUzODg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4525388?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zireael07","html_url":"https://github.com/Zireael07","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zireael07/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zireael07/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zireael07/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zireael07/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zireael07/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zireael07/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zireael07/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zireael07/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zireael07/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-04T13:58:44Z","updated_at":"2024-11-04T13:58:44Z","body":"Nit: I'd change the title to be \"very large\", as \"deep\" usually refers to the scene tree's complexity","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2454789078/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2861340880","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/98655#issuecomment-2861340880","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98655","id":2861340880,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6qjJjQ","user":{"login":"CodeSmith32","id":21373557,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMzczNTU3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21373557?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/CodeSmith32","html_url":"https://github.com/CodeSmith32","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CodeSmith32/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CodeSmith32/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CodeSmith32/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CodeSmith32/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CodeSmith32/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CodeSmith32/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CodeSmith32/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CodeSmith32/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CodeSmith32/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-08T02:29:22Z","updated_at":"2025-05-08T02:29:22Z","body":"Around 1 million units from the origin, large amounts of snapping and popping occur in the standard Godot build.\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/977958e3-f17a-476d-8f6f-b775ffdcbae0\n\nShort of using the double-precision build of Godot and the [two-float breakdown trick described here](https://godotengine.org/article/emulating-double-precision-gpu-render-large-worlds/#the-real-solution), there is only one workaround I know, but it does significantly increase the complexity of most projects (it also doesn't work in the editor, though that's slightly less important):\n\n1. Move the world, not the camera.\n2. Use multiple layers of coordinates for computing the player's 'virtual' position (really, the world's negative position).\n  - e.g., Use one Vector3 for coordinates within a 4,096^3 unit region, and a Vector3i which indicates which region the player is in.\n\nUnfortunately, this is much easier said than done:\n- Placing everything under a node and simply setting the node's position to the camera's negative position will probably have a similar effect on movement (and naturally so, since the float-based transform hits the same limits).\n- Worse (please correct me if I'm wrong), in my experience, moving the world seriously screws with Godot's physics engine. Since physics run in a separate thread, I believe, when moving the world, sometimes only half the objects' physical bodies move within a physics frame. Thus, using any kind of snapping or jumping - like wrapping the player camera in a cell indexed by a Vector3i, and jumping the world when wrap occurs - would cause bodies to collide when they shouldn't, and at times that are unpredictable and very difficult to track.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2861340880/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3038784064","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/98655#issuecomment-3038784064","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98655","id":3038784064,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc61ICpA","user":{"login":"Flarkk","id":49606622,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5NjA2NjIy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/49606622?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk","html_url":"https://github.com/Flarkk","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-05T11:12:43Z","updated_at":"2025-07-05T12:18:50Z","body":"@CodeSmith32 you're indeed pointing out the right two options :\n- use the double-precision build\n- or implement a \"floating origin\" system, i.e. leave the camera near the origin and move the rest of the world instead\n\nThe latter cannot be implemented by putting everything under a node and moving it to the camera's negative location. As you pointed out it would lead to the same numerical precision issues.\n\nThe simplest valid implementation I can think of is to derive a custom node type from `Node3D` that stores its real-world position as 3 `float` member variables (note that the `float` type is always 64 bits even in the single-precision build). Each frame, this node uses these 3 `float` to compute its relative real-world vector to the camera (another instance of this custom node also using 3 `floats` for positioning) and moves all its children accordingly using their built-in position. Create as much of these custom nodes as needed and parent your scene's objects to them with respect to their desired real-world position (assign objects that are too far apart to distinct parents).\n\nIf you're using physics, you'll have to provide a mechanism that ensures that this custom node type updates its physics children through their `_integrate_forces()` method. This is where you can access their `PhysicsDirectBodyState3D` and safely change their `transform` to arbitrary values without side effect.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3038784064/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3394307713","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/98655#issuecomment-3394307713","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98655","id":3394307713,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7KUQaB","user":{"login":"ARez2","id":75789249,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc1Nzg5MjQ5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/75789249?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ARez2","html_url":"https://github.com/ARez2","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ARez2/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ARez2/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ARez2/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ARez2/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ARez2/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ARez2/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ARez2/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ARez2/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ARez2/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-12T12:28:41Z","updated_at":"2025-10-12T12:28:41Z","body":"My issue ( #111521 ) might be related, but not sure","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3394307713/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3395205483","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/98655#issuecomment-3395205483","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98655","id":3395205483,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7KXrlr","user":{"login":"CodeSmith32","id":21373557,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMzczNTU3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21373557?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/CodeSmith32","html_url":"https://github.com/CodeSmith32","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CodeSmith32/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CodeSmith32/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CodeSmith32/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CodeSmith32/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CodeSmith32/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CodeSmith32/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CodeSmith32/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CodeSmith32/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CodeSmith32/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-12T18:35:00Z","updated_at":"2025-10-12T18:35:00Z","body":"> or implement a \"floating origin\" system, i.e. leave the camera near the origin and move the rest of the world instead\n\n@Flarkk, I have yet to try this solution, but it sounds promising!","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3395205483/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]